Inkling 2 Small expert-split recipe
======================================

Part of dgx-station-recipes (MIT; see ../LICENSE). Copyright 2026 Tomas Cupr.
The hot-on-GB300 / cold-on-RTX / spill-to-Grace shape follows Garner McCloud's
deepseek-v4.1-flash recipe. This directory does not copy his kernels: those
are MXFP4 for DeepSeek. The CUDA here is new, uncompiled, and marked
UNVALIDATED.

The checkpoint is thinkingmachines/Inkling-2-Small revision
8361e7a31ae7e9966a49a91d3994fde618936c2b. This repository does not redistribute
the weights.

Expert numerics (E2M1 nibble order, E4M3, amax/2688, activation amax/1536,
fouroversix_mae, UE8M0, interleaved w13, softcapped SwiGLU, sigmoid-bias
top-8) were read from vLLM pull request 67325 at d664cd1e, file
vllm/models/inkling2/, which is Apache-2.0, Copyright contributors to the
vLLM project. The numpy in kernels/reference/quant.py is a reimplementation
of those formulas, not a copy of that source. The denominator 2688 was also
read from four bytes of layer 0's w13_weight_outer_scale_denominator (the
value is 2688.0). 1536 is the constant in that vLLM file's `_row_scales`,
not a value stored in the checkpoint.
